Application (i.e Authentication framework like Spring Security) pehle user ko authenticate karti hai
(i.e. verify karti hai ki username/password ya credentials valid hain ya nahi).

Authentication successful hone ke baad application generally HttpSession create karti hai (through the Servlet Container such as Tomcat).

Tomcat us session ko ek unique Session ID assign karta hai.

Ye mapping internally maintain ki jaati hai:

        Session ID
             ↓
     HttpSession Object


Tomcat internally ek Session Manager maintain karta hai,
jisme Session ID aur uske corresponding HttpSession Object
ki mapping stored hoti hai.


